<title>JAPAN: TSE allows Sony, 19 others to list stock options.</title>
<headline>TSE allows Sony, 19 others to list stock options.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) said on Monday that it would allow Sony Corp, Nissan Motor Co Ltd, Canon Inc and 17 other firms to list stock options that are scheduled to start trading on July 18.  </p>
<p>The 17 other firms are as follows:</p>
<p>Taisei Corp</p>
<p>Kirin Brewery Co Ltd</p>
<p>Toray Industries Inc</p>
<p>Sankyo Co Ltd</p>
<p>Fuji Photo Film Co Ltd</p>
<p>Nippon Steel Corp</p>
<p>Komatsu Ltd</p>
<p>Hitachi Ltd</p>
<p>Denso Corp</p>
<p>Ricoh Co Ltd</p>
<p>Dai Nippon Printing Co Ltd</p>
<p>Sega Enterprises Ltd</p>
<p>Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd</p>
<p>Seven-Eleven Japan Co Ltd</p>
<p>Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd</p>
<p>Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd</p>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc</p>
</text>
